From: OCCTSwift ecosystem <noreply@secondmouse.au>
Subject: [PATCH] Modeling Data - GProp_SelGProps returns cos(semiAngle) times
 the lateral area of a gp_Cone

GProp_SelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone&, ...) computes

  double Auxi1 = R + (Z2 + Z1) * Snt / 2.;
  dim          = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1) * Auxi1;

gp_Cone's v parameter runs along the generatrix:

  P(u, v) = Loc + (R + v sin a)(cos u X + sin u Y) + v cos a Z

so dP/du = (R + v sin a)(-sin u X + cos u Y) and dP/dv = sin a (cos u X +
sin u Y) + cos a Z. The two are orthogonal, |dP/du| is R + v sin a and |dP/dv|
is 1, so the area element is

  |dP/du ^ dP/dv| du dv = (R + v sin a) du dv

and the lateral area over u in [Alpha1, Alpha2], v in [Z1, Z2] is

  A = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) (Z2 - Z1) (R + (Z2 + Z1) sin a / 2)

which is Auxi1 times (Alpha2 - Alpha1) (Z2 - Z1). The Cnt factor has no term to
come from, and dim is therefore A cos(a). No reading of Z saves it: were Z the
axial coordinate rather than the slant, the correction would be a division by
cos(a), not a multiplication. The factor goes to 1 as a goes to 0, which is why
the gp_Cylinder overload beside it, dim = R (Z2 - Z1) (Alpha2 - Alpha1), is
exact and never showed this.

The centre of mass in the same function is already right and is untouched:
Iz = Cnt (R (Z2 + Z1) / 2 + Snt Auxi2) / Auxi1 is the first moment of the same
area element divided by Auxi1, so it is independent of how dim is scaled.

GProp_SelGProps and GProp_VelGProps have no caller anywhere in the OCCT tree,
so there is no call site whose use of the result could settle the convention.
The arbiters are therefore the closed form above and the cylinder limit: a cone
of vanishing semi-angle is the cylinder that the same class answers exactly, and
with this change it converges on it.

Measured on macOS arm64 against V8_0_1 with the translation unit
override-linked, gp_Cone(gp::XOY(), pi/6, 5) over u in [0, 2 pi], v in [0, 10].
Before: Mass() is 408.10485695269909 against the closed form 471.23889803846896,
a ratio of 0.86602540378443882 where cos(pi/6) is 0.86602540378443871. After:
Mass() is 471.23889803846896, equal to the closed form to the last bit, the
centre of mass is unchanged at (0, 0, 4.81125224325), and the near-cylinder
cases at semiAngle 1e-3, 1e-6 and 1e-9 converge on the cylinder's
314.15926535897933.

The inertia terms below dim carry a separate discrepancy of their own, measured
but deliberately not touched here: Dm(3, 3) comes out cos(a) sin(a) times the
second moment about the axis. That is a distinct defect with its own derivation
and no measurement behind it in a caller, and fixing it here would change a
second result under cover of this one.

The reproducer is Scripts/repro/2992/probe.cxx and the transcript is
Scripts/repro/2992/override-link-transcript.txt in the OCCTSwift repository.
OCCTSwift issue #2992; the volume half of the same issue is patch 0051.

diff --git a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx
--- a/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx
+++ b/src/ModelingData/TKGeomBase/GProp/GProp_SelGProps.cxx
@@ -122,7 +122,8 @@ void GProp_SelGProps::Perform(const gp_Cone& S,

   double Auxi1 = R + (Z2 + Z1) * Snt / 2.;
   double Auxi2 = (Z2 * Z2 + Z1 * Z2 + Z1 * Z1) / 3.;
-  dim          = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * Cnt * (Z2 - Z1) * Auxi1;
+  // |dP/du ^ dP/dv| is R + v sin(a) on gp_Cone, so the area carries no cos(a) factor.
+  dim = (Alpha2 - Alpha1) * (Z2 - Z1) * Auxi1;

   double Ix = (R * R + R * (Z2 + Z1) * Snt + Snt * Auxi2) / Auxi1;
   double Iy = Ix * (Cn1 - Cn2) / (Alpha2 - Alpha1);
